database  The  command  creates  a database in which contains the
names of all of the character and  block  special  files  in  the
specified  directory,  using  the  file type and the field as the
key.  If no directory is specified, the directory is used.   Keys
are a structure containing a mode_t followed by a dev_t, with any
padding  zero’d out.  The former is the type of the file (st_mode
& S_IFMT), the latter is the st_rdev field.  The options  are  as
follows:  Create  a database for compatibility with libc versions
and statically linked programs from before The  default  name  is
Put  the  output  databases in the named file.  Device directory.
